<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Orlam Afrikaner State</h1><p class="st-meta">1823 CE – 1880 CE (approx.) · capital Windhoek</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Jonker Afrikaner's horse-riding, gun-using Oorlam state that dominated central Namibia and founded Windhoek.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaners">Afrikaners</a> were an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oorlam">Oorlam</a> group, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khoekhoe">Khoekhoe</a> of the Cape frontier who had adopted horses, guns and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-dutch">Cape Dutch</a>, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jager-afrikaner">Jager Afrikaner</a>. Around 1823 his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jonker-afrikaner">Jonker Afrikaner</a> moved north at the invitation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nama-people">Nama</a> to help them against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herero-people">Herero</a>, and by about 1840 he had settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/windhoek">Windhoek</a>, which he made his capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jonker-afrikaner">Jonker</a>'s mounted gunmen raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herero-people">Herero</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and controlled trade routes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walvis-bay">Walvis Bay</a>, where cattle were exchanged for guns, horses and brandy. He welcomed Wesleyan and Rhenish missionaries, built a road to the coast and ruled a large following of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oorlam">Oorlam</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nama-people">Nama</a> and dependent Herero. His power rested on firearms and alliances rather than on a fixed territory.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jonker-afrikaner">Jonker</a>'s death in 1861 and his son Christian's death in battle at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otjimbingwe">Otjimbingwe</a> in 1863, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herero-people">Herero</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharero">Maharero</a> won their independence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-jonker-afrikaner">Jan Jonker Afrikaner</a> was finally defeated by the Herero in 1880, and the group lost its land.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1823 CE – 1880 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.98%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1823 CE – 1880 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Windhoek</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jager Afrikaner, Jonker Afrikaner, Jan Jonker Afrikaner</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity, Khoekhoe traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Khoekhoe, Cape Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/namibia">Namibia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Jonker Afrikaner's state, Afrikaner Oorlams</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1852&amp;focus=orlam-afrikaner-state" aria-label="Orlam Afrikaner State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5137 3011 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Orlam Afrikaner State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5457 3267L5454 3246"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5454 3246h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5457 3267h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5457 3267h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Windhoek. <a href="/atlas?year=1852&amp;focus=orlam-afrikaner-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
